  <phrase title="option.dcLoginAsUser_suppress" version_id="1000070" version_string="1.0.0"><![CDATA[Hide the visit from the impersonated account]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.dcLoginAsUser_logLength" version_id="1000070" version_string="1.0.0"><![CDATA[In days. Completed sessions older than this are deleted. Sessions that are still open are never deleted, whatever their age. Enter 0 to keep the log forever.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.dcLoginAsUser_maxDuration" version_id="1000070" version_string="1.0.0"><![CDATA[In minutes. A staff member is returned to their own account automatically once this long has passed. Enter 0 for no limit. The value in force is fixed when a session starts, so changing this does not lengthen or shorten a session that is already running. Note that XenForo's own session lifetime is a fixed 4 hours, so values above 240 can never be reached.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.dcLoginAsUser_requirePassword" version_id="1000070" version_string="1.0.0"><![CDATA[Staff must re-enter their own password before taking over an account. A confirmation lasts 30 minutes, and taking over an account clears it again - so each impersonation is confirmed separately. Leaving this on means a stolen staff session is not by itself enough to access member accounts.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_explain.dcLoginAsUser_suppress" version_id="1000070" version_string="1.0.0"><![CDATA[Anything left ticked is suppressed while a staff member is signed in as another member, so the visit does not show up in that member's own account. Untick an item to let it behave normally. Note that "Currently online list" and "Last activity time" are the same underlying record in XenForo, so suppressing the first also freezes the second.]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_group.dcLoginAsUser" version_id="1010070" version_string="1.1.0"><![CDATA[D.C Style - Login as user]]></phrase>
  <phrase title="option_group_description.dcLoginAsUser" version_id="1000070" version_string="1.0.0"><![CDATA[Controls how long a staff member may stay signed in as another member, how long the audit log is kept, and how much of a trace the impersonated account is left with.]]></phrase>
